# Droopy Agent QA rule

If `.droopy/onboarding.json` is missing or `.env` still has placeholders, follow `droopy-onboarding.mdc` first. Do not start QA until onboarding is complete.

Follow `AGENTS.md` as the execution contract.

- One Chrome DevTools MCP process with `$HOME/.droopy-agent/chrome-profile` unless `DROOPY_CHROME_PROFILE` is set. Serial: one review item at a time. Do not launch a second chrome-devtools server or `--userDataDir`. Do not use `--isolated` (wipes SSO). Sub-agents reuse the parent browser.
- Save screenshots as `evidence/<ticket-or-id>-<what>.png` (absolute workspace path). Never `/tmp`, Desktop, or home dumps; retry `evidence/` only on write failure. Attach from `evidence/` when the tracker accepts files.
- Reload the configured queue (`QA_QUEUE_URL`) at the start of every QA session. Do not pick items from a stale leftover tab.
- Derive a checklist from every acceptance criterion before testing.
- Prefer exact linked Figma evidence via headless Figma MCP; when absent, use `DESIGN.md`, live consistency, and accessibility.
- Pass requires positive evidence for every applicable requirement. Incomplete testing is not Pass.
- Loading or hang may be session state: wait, then SSO retry. Fail only after that retry still fails.
- Persistence tests: after changing filters or state, click the client's persist-commit control (`QA_PERSIST_COMMIT_LABEL`) before judging save. If that label is empty, skip persist-commit and record that it was not configured.
- Pass/Fail on the tracker comment when comments exist; skip the results sheet when `QA_RESULTS_SHEET_URL` is empty; if neither exists, write `evidence/<ticket-or-id>-result.md`. Use `QA_TRACKER_TYPE` as configured — do not invent Jira fields or spreadsheet columns.
- One result comment on the ticket. If we were wrong, edit that comment; do not stack. Never overwrite other people's defects or comments.
- For failures, follow `docs/BUG-CREATION.md`. If a matching defect already exists, log it and stop.
- Tracker and app live in Chrome DevTools. Optional GitHub or Mural MCP only if the operator added them.
- Ask only when blocked (Cursor: AskQuestion). Never expose credentials, cookies, or tokens. SSO using emails in `.env` only — no passwords.
